To expand means to remove the brackets. In {'(x + ' + 2 + ')(x + ' + 5 + ')'} each term of the first bracket multiplies each term of the second:
• x × x = x²
• x × {5} = {mono(5, 'x')}
• {2} × x = {mono(2, 'x')}
• {2} × {5} = {10}
Four products. Then collect the like terms: {poly([1, 'x²'], [7, 'x'], [10, ''])}.
Signs come with their terms: in {'(x + ' + 3 + ')(x − ' + 4 + ')'} the products are x², {mono(-4, 'x')}, {mono(3, 'x')} and {-12}, giving {poly([1, 'x²'], [-1, 'x'], [-12, ''])}.
